    {
      "id": "claim_f179961a3d2b48dd8ba40fc530cc4cc5",
      "statement": "The overwrite release (`-o`) probes the remote, plans an update to an existing non-draft Release whose tag equals `v{version}`, then backs up replaced assets, edits notes, and re-uploads per asset with failed-asset restore — without bumping the version, moving the tag, or creating a commit.",
